  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is the best time to visit Teerathgarh Falls?",
      "a": "October to March is the best time: the falls are full from monsoon runoff and the weather is cool (12–28°C). Avoid peak summer (Apr–Jun) when flows reduce."
    },
    {
      "q": "How far is Teerathgarh Falls from Jagdalpur?",
      "a": "Teerathgarh Falls is about 35–38 km south of Jagdalpur on the Sukma highway, inside Kanger Valley National Park. Takes around 45–60 minutes by road."
    },
    {
      "q": "What are the top places to visit near Teerathgarh Falls?",
      "a": "Top attractions include Kotumsar Cave (9 km), Kailash Gufa cave shrine (5 km), Chitrakote Waterfalls — Niagara of India (48 km), and Kanger Valley National Park forest trails."
    },
    {
      "q": "Are there good hotels near Teerathgarh Falls?",
      "a": "Accommodation ranges from eco-jungle resorts (₹5400+/night) to budget OYO-style stays (from ₹900/night), mostly in Jagdalpur, the closest major town at 35 km."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is an entry fee required for Teerathgarh Falls?",
      "a": "Yes, there is a nominal entry fee for Kanger Valley National Park (around ₹100) which covers access to Teerathgarh Falls and Kotumsar Cave."
    }
  ],
